.TH SNX 1 "2026-07-19" "Silent Nexus 1.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
snx \- local-first agentic CLI with controlled execution
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B snx
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.br
.B snx run
[\fB--agent\fR \fIROLE\fR] \fIOBJECTIVE\fR
.br
.B snx maintenance
\fBcheck\fR|\fBbackup\fR|\fBoptimize\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Silent Nexus treats the model as an untrusted planner. The Rust harness
validates tool schemas, capabilities, workspace paths, policy, approvals,
sandbox metadata, output limits, secret redaction, and audit records before
and after execution.
.PP
The 1.3.0 release tooling targets x86_64 GNU/Linux. Certification requires a
completed release report; other platforms are experimental until independently
tested.
.SH COMMON COMMANDS
.TP
.B snx
Launch the interactive terminal interface.
.TP
.B snx setup
Discover local model servers and create a starter configuration.
.TP
.B snx run \(dqOBJECTIVE\(dq
Run one non-interactive objective.
.TP
.B snx doctor --deep
Check configuration, state integrity, permissions, WAL, artifacts, release
metadata, isolation posture, and current-binary integrity.
.TP
.B snx maintenance check
Check SQLite integrity, permissions, WAL state, storage size, migration
checksums, and artifact hashes without deleting data.
.TP
.B snx maintenance backup DIRECTORY
Create an atomic SQLite and artifact snapshot with a SHA-256 manifest. The
destination must not already exist.
.TP
.B snx maintenance optimize [--vacuum]
Run PRAGMA optimize and checkpoint the WAL. VACUUM is optional and is refused
while foreground or background work is active.
.TP
.B snx sandbox status
Report the actual isolation backend and its limitations.
.TP
.B snx completion SHELL
Generate completions for bash, zsh, fish, elvish, or PowerShell.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Emit machine-readable output where supported.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable color. The NO_COLOR environment variable is also honored.
.TP
.B --inline
Run the TUI without the alternate screen.
.TP
.B -v, --verbose
Increase log verbosity.
.SH ISOLATION
Container execution is strong isolation for the 1.x contract: commands run as
the invoking UID/GID with a read-only root filesystem, per-action workspace
access, private-path masks, network disabled by default, dropped capabilities,
and resource limits.
.PP
The process backend is an approval-only host guardrail, not containment. Every
model-proposed terminal action requires a prominent one-time attended approval,
and background or unattended terminal execution is denied.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .nexus/config.toml
Workspace configuration.
.TP
.I .nexus/state/nexus.db
Workspace SQLite database.
.TP
.I .nexus/state/artifacts/
Content-addressed durable artifacts.
.TP
.I ~/.config/silent-nexus/config.toml
User configuration on Linux, subject to XDG_CONFIG_HOME.
.TP
.I ~/.config/silent-nexus/auth/
Private provider credential profiles.
.SH SECURITY
Generic model filesystem tools cannot access .nexus, .git, common credential
paths, private keys, or credential stores. Generic terminal privilege
escalation and Git commit, push, remote, alias, or unrecognized operations are
denied. Use audited typed workflows.
.PP
Report vulnerabilities privately through:
.UR https://github.com/Silent-Protocol-Inc/Silent-Nexus-Agents/security/advisories/new
.UE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR docker (1),
.BR podman (1)
.PP
Full documentation is in the Silent Nexus README and docs directory.
